From: ViKing <viking.yfy@qq.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 14:06:01 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: ath12k: release firmware at core teardown

Core pre-init maps the API2 container before PCI IRQ, MHI, HAL and CE
setup can fail. PCI probe unwind and AHB removal both free the core
without passing through the old PCI-only firmware release. Release the
container with its core owner, after bus resources and workqueues stop.
Keep firmware pointers valid for MHI teardown and recovery.

Signed-off-by: ViKing <viking.yfy@qq.com>
---
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/core.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/core.c
@@ -2368,6 +2368,7 @@ void ath12k_core_free(struct ath12k_base
 	ath12k_wmi_free();
 	destroy_workqueue(ab->workqueue_aux);
 	destroy_workqueue(ab->workqueue);
+	ath12k_fw_unmap(ab);
 	kfree(ab);
 }
 
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/pci.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/pci.c
@@ -1724,7 +1724,6 @@ static void ath12k_pci_remove(struct pci
 
 qmi_fail:
 	ath12k_core_deinit(ab);
-	ath12k_fw_unmap(ab);
 	ath12k_mhi_unregister(ab_pci);
 
 	ath12k_pci_free_irq(ab);
